Derived data for the LRG samples from

Cosmological constraints from the tomographic cross-correlation of DESI
Luminous Red Galaxies and Planck CMB lensing
Martin White, et al.
https://arxiv.org/abs/2111.09898

Samples s01 through s04 correspond to pz_bin 1 through 4.  Files like
lrg_s01_cls.txt contain galaxy-galaxy and galaxy-kappa spectra:

cls: Contain the galaxy auto-spectra and galaxy-kappa cross-spectra.
cov: The combined auto- and cross-spectrum covariance matrix (see file header).
dndz:The (normalized) redshift distribution for the photo-z sample.
mod: A smooth model, used to compute the covariance matrix.
wla: The window function matrix for the auto-spectra.
wlx: The window function matrix for the cross-spectra.


while files like lrg_s01_s02_* represent galaxy cross-spectra between
pz_bins (in this case s01 and s02).
